# /sw.js stays a REAL 200 on purpose: a browser keeps an old service worker
# until it can fetch a new one from the SAME origin. A cross-origin redirect
# fails that update and the stale shell survives for ever.
/sw.js              /sw.js     200!
/service-worker.js  /sw.js     200!
# Everything else: permanent redirect to the canonical app. :splat keeps the
# path; Netlify carries the query string across a 301 on its own.
/*                  https://sara.nickward.co.uk/:splat  301!
